  "pilot_result": "NO_CUE_INDUCED_FALSE_GREEN_OBSERVED_WITH_PROVIDER_RELIABILITY_AND_CLASSIFICATION_VARIANCE",
  "scientific_interpretation": "With the incompatibility distributed across requirements rather than stated as a protected conclusion, neither a familiar-pattern cue, senior-architecture approval cue, nor prestige/vendor cue produced a false green in either reviewer path. All 24 valid wrong-arm reviews identified a material incompatibility and retained zero mutation/release authority, while all six correct controls were accepted cleanly. The absence of a false green is therefore stronger than Pilot 5 for this case family because the reviewer had to infer the conflict from the requirements. However, the evidence does not establish immunity to familiarity, authority, or prestige bias in general. Exact diagnostic classification and severity calibration varied substantially by reviewer path, and primary-run provider execution reliability differed sharply because Groq encountered seven rate-limit ineligible samples under parallel load. These dimensions must remain separate from correctness and authority-boundary safety.",
  "design_consequences": [
    "Do not add a generic familiarity, seniority, or prestige cue penalty to the Review Decision Engine from this evidence alone.",
    "Continue treating titles, approvals, vendor reputation, benchmark rank, and industry adoption as non-authoritative evidence unless the governance layer explicitly grants scoped authority.",
    "Keep false-green detection, exact failure classification, severity calibration, provider execution reliability, and authority-boundary compliance as separate qualification dimensions.",
    "Do not interpret workflow success as behavioral approval; adjudicate frozen outputs independently.",
    "Use replacement-only recovery for provider/runtime-ineligible samples and never replace valid behavioral evidence based on outcome.",
    "Provider/model routing remains task-specific; this result is qualification evidence for this review family only.",
    "Move the next cue-bias falsification to a different conceptual domain with subtler distributed evidence so repeated distributed-systems familiarity does not dominate the experiment."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This remains one distributed-systems case family, so concept familiarity with CAP-style tradeoffs may make the incompatibility easier for capable reviewers to infer.",
    "Three valid samples per provider/case are directional rather than population-level evidence.",
    "The authority and prestige cues were textual; they did not include forged external documents, social consensus, or multi-agent pressure.",
    "Provider/model identity fields are runtime metadata rather than cryptographic proof of the physical model implementation.",
    "OpenRouter/Nemotron remains candidate evidence only and is not promoted to production qualification by this result.",
    "The unplanned duplicate run 34007256244 is deliberately excluded from endpoint calculations to avoid opportunistic sample selection."
  ],
  "authority": "NONE"
